PART 3 -- s_ph AND THE DECISION SIGMA (Monte-Carlo propagated)
====================================================================================================
  s_ph(task)     = (M_tot - M_bar - M_gas)/M_tot   [the dark share, M_bar = f_star, M_gas = f_gas]
  s_ph^eq(pi)    = f_b / u,  u = r_M/R500 = sqrt(G M_b/a0)/R500   [the pie's equipartition phantom, G179 identity]
  f_dust(missing)= 1 - s_ph^eq/(1 - s_b)   [G178's falsifier: < 0.85 voids the all-dust/sharp reading]


  A1644 (M500 = 3.48e+14):
    pie curve at this mass: s_b = 0.144; SHARP s_ph = 0.527; SMOOTH s_ph = 0.527  (branch separation 0.000)
    s_ph(task-formula, dark share)      = 0.856 (16-84 [0.845, 0.866])
    s_ph^eq (equipartition phantom)      = 0.658 (16-84 [0.596, 0.740])
    f_dust(missing) = 1 - s_ph^eq/(1-s_b)= 0.268 (16-84 [0.195, 0.322])   [falsifier < 0.85: FIRES (smooth)]
    DECISION: s_ph^eq vs SMOOTH at +1.82 sigma, vs SHARP at +1.82 sigma -> INDECISIVE (grey)

  Hydra A (A780) (M500 = 2.21e+14):
    pie curve at this mass: s_b = 0.089; SHARP s_ph = 0.089; SMOOTH s_ph = 0.188  (branch separation 0.100)
